  "explanation": "The theorem says conjugation by x commutes with the commutator. Mathlib's `map_commutatorElement` says any monoid hom class element f satisfies f ⁅a, b⁆ = ⁅f a, f b⁆. Take f = `MulAut.conj x`. `MulAut.conj_apply` is `rfl` and gives `conj x u = x * u * x⁻¹`, so the statement is the same up to defeq. If the term doesn't elaborate directly, `by simpa using map_commutatorElement (MulAut.conj x) u v` should work. I found no Mathlib lemma stating the conjugation form directly. The library's own proof unfolds the commutator and calls `group`, so it doesn't use `map_commutatorElement`.",
